WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.040
Few games have promised and then delivered&nbsp;
as much mayhem as Borderlands, the loot ‘em&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:11.280
up from Gearbox Software. With a spin-off of the&nbsp;
series on the horizon, Tiny Tina’s Wonderlands,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.920
we decided it was time to take a look&nbsp;
back, so here’s the History of Borderlands.&nbsp;

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:24.320
In 2007, Gearbox Software had some&nbsp;
interesting projects in the works.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:28.960
They were in pre-production on a game based&nbsp;
on the movie Aliens, wonder what happened to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:34.000
that one, and were apparently in talks with&nbsp;
director Michael Mann to make a Heat game.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:43.360
The team was also deep in production on&nbsp;
another title, a hybrid first-person shooter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:49.120
and role-playing game called Borderlands. The team&nbsp;
were familiar with making first-person shooters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:54.640
after working on expansion packs for Half-Life,&nbsp;
as well as the PC port of Halo: Combat Evolved,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.640 --> 00:01:00.240
but wanted to combine their knowledge of making&nbsp;
FPS games with their love of loot grinding in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:06.720
games like Diablo to create a shooter “that&nbsp;
would have loot coming out of every orifice”.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:13.360
The game was revealed via the September 2007 Game&nbsp;
Informer cover, and even during this first look,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:17.760
the ambition was clear. The game was&nbsp;
built for co-op in mind from the start,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:21.680
with players taking control of one&nbsp;
of the three playable characters:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:27.760
Roland, Mordecai, and Lillith, and playing solo,&nbsp;
with AI, or with up to three others online or in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:33.440
split-screen co-op. There were vehicles to drive&nbsp;
around the expansive wastes of the planet Pandora,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:37.200
numerous skills to unlock, and&nbsp;
to scratch that looting itch,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:43.520
Gearbox boasted over 500,000 unique weapons which&nbsp;
would be procedurally generated for players.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:01.120
While the Game Informer article offered a few&nbsp;
images of the game, the first trailer wouldn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:05.520
arrive until almost a year later at E3 2008&nbsp;
(Borderlands First Trailer), and compared to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:12.240
the whacky, colourful Borderlands we know today,&nbsp;
the Borderlands of 2008 was… dare I say it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:24.080
a little generic looking. And it seemed that&nbsp;
Gearbox knew it. Testers kept comparing the game&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:30.000
to iD Software’s Rage, and the recently released&nbsp;
Fallout 3, and there was a clashing of themes:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.120
the gameplay was ridiculous and over the top,&nbsp;
but the visuals suggested gritty realism.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:40.960
The team was 75% of the way through the&nbsp;
project and didn’t have the money to reboot it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:45.200
so the team switched up the art style&nbsp;
to look more like ink-lined comic books,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:50.320
and scrapped the “boring” abilities from&nbsp;
the skill trees, emphasising the whackier&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:54.960
ones. The new art style was such a hit,&nbsp;
but an awful lot of work to implement,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.960 --> 00:03:03.840
so Gearbox employees from other games started&nbsp;
helping out on Borderlands in their spare time.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:10.960
Borderlands launched in October 2009,&nbsp;
shoulder to shoulder with juggernauts like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:17.440
Uncharted 2, Halo 3: ODST, and Modern&nbsp;
Warfare 2, but was a surprise hit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:22.720
with Xbox 360 copies even selling out in&nbsp;
many stores on the East Coast of the US.

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:28.000
Praise was heaped upon its gameplay, which was at&nbsp;
its best when players grouped up to play together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:32.320
with players finding the loop of shooting&nbsp;
enemies, gathering loot, and levelling up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:37.360
intensely satisfying: there was always another&nbsp;
enemy to shoot, another new gun to get,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:42.400
and another skill to unlock. Each of the now four&nbsp;
Vault Hunters offered their own unique powers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:48.080
that would sing when played together with friends&nbsp;
in co-op. Death didn’t necessarily mean the end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:52.640
either, if you were downed in battle, killing&nbsp;
another enemy would give you a second wind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:57.680
pushing you back into the fight. The new art&nbsp;
style worked in its favour, making the expansive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:02.480
world of Pandora visually appealing and more&nbsp;
in line with the game’s over the top nature.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:06.640
Less positively received was the game’s&nbsp;
story, which was described as “thin” in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:11.520
our review. Players would take control of one&nbsp;
of four Vault Hunters who would scour Pandora,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:16.800
an almost barren planet that had been picked&nbsp;
over by one of the universe’s many corporations,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:20.160
to find key fragments that,&nbsp;
when combined would unlock a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:25.120
Vault full of untold riches on the planet.&nbsp;
Helping you out on your quest is Claptrap,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:33.600
an… excitable robot who would unfortunately&nbsp;
go on to become the mascot for the series.

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:48.320
Borderlands received four pieces of downloadable&nbsp;
content, and while they offered the usual:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:53.600
new missions, areas, weapons, and enemies, they&nbsp;
also acted as a testbed for the developers to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:58.320
try out new ideas. Borderlands sold&nbsp;
2 million copies in just two months,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:03.440
high numbers for a new IP pushing its way to&nbsp;
market during the busiest time of year, and while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:09.840
a sequel was “a no-brainer” according to Gearbox,&nbsp;
it took them a few years to actually announce it.&nbsp;

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:20.400
In August 2011, publisher 2K and Gearbox&nbsp;
officially revealed Borderlands 2,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:24.880
and while initial details were scant, Gearbox&nbsp;
promised that the sequel would be bigger and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:30.560
better than the first game, offering new character&nbsp;
classes, weapons, enemies, and areas to explore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:36.240
as well as an “ambitiously crafted story”. At&nbsp;
Gamescom that year, Gearbox offered a glimpse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:41.520
of what that meant: the game’s weapon system&nbsp;
had been replaced, the AI had been improved,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:46.080
more voice acting had been added, and the&nbsp;
quest and vehicle systems had been overhauled.

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:51.760
The thin story had been heavily criticised in&nbsp;
the first game, so in order to create a better&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:56.880
connection between the gameplay of Borderlands and&nbsp;
its story, the lead designer and the lead writer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.880 --> 00:06:02.240
worked more closely together for Borderlands&nbsp;
2. The goal was to make a story so ridiculous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:06.560
that it would be beyond criticism, something&nbsp;
to fit the nature of the gameplay itself.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:12.080
One of the biggest changes came with the cast&nbsp;
of playable characters, the four original Vault&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:18.400
Hunters were replaced with Axton, Maya, Salvador,&nbsp;
and Zer0, with two more launching later as DLC.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:22.800
But that didn’t mean the end of the original&nbsp;
Vault Hunters, they returned as NPCs and quest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:27.680
givers in the game, a nice nod for those who got&nbsp;
attached while playing Borderlands 1. The new and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:33.040
old heroes were teaming up against Handsome Jack,&nbsp;
the charming president of the nefarious Hyperion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:38.000
Corporation who brings his forces to Pandora&nbsp;
hoping to open another Vault on the planet.

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:48.880
Gearbox promised a bigger, better sequel, and&nbsp;
boy did they deliver. Fans loved exploring the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:55.120
more expansive, exciting world of Pandora and all&nbsp;
of the new opportunities for mayhem it presented.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:59.920
Reviewers praised the writing, in particular&nbsp;
new characters like Tiny Tina, but more from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:11.200
her in a bit. But Borderlands 2 wasn’t without&nbsp;
its controversies. Before the game launched, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:15.360
developers caught flak for referring to the&nbsp;
Mechromancer’s skilltree as the “girlfriend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:19.760
mode” for lesser skilled players, with its&nbsp;
actual name being Best Friends Forever.

00:07:19.760 --> 00:07:24.880
In the UK, Borderlands 2 was the most&nbsp;
pre-ordered 2K game ever, and by 2014,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:31.280
it became the highest-selling 2K game in history,&nbsp;
selling well over 12 million copies by 2015.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:35.600
It came as no surprise then, that Hollywood&nbsp;
came knocking, with Lionsgate announcing a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:41.360
film of the series in 2016. While it still&nbsp;
hasn’t been released as of early 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:46.640
huge names like Jamie Lee Curtis, Cate&nbsp;
Blanchett, and Jack Black are attached to star.

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:49.920
Borderlands 2 had a number of&nbsp;
pieces of downloadable content,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:54.720
including new Vault Hunters Gaige the&nbsp;
Mechromancer and Krieg the Psycho. 2013's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.720 --> 00:08:00.080
Tiny Tina’s Assault on Dragon Keep was a vast&nbsp;
departure from the story of the vault hunters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:04.400
where Tina ran a tabletop game of&nbsp;
Bunkers and Badasses–the Pandora&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:09.920
take on Dungeons &amp; Dragons–and the Vault Hunters&nbsp;
would father as a party to rescue Butt Stallion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:15.520
from the evil Handsome Sorcerer. The pack was well&nbsp;
received, later being released as a standalone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:25.840
one-shot in 2021, and serving as the inspiration&nbsp;
for the spin off game, Tiny Tina’s Wonderlands.

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:33.280
After the release of the wildly successful&nbsp;
Borderlands 2, Gearbox began working with 2K&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:38.240
Australia to make a prequel that would bridge&nbsp;
the story and explain how Handsome Jack rose to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:43.280
power in the first place. The majority of&nbsp;
production was conducted by 2K Australia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:48.480
but certain key team members like the writers of&nbsp;
Borderlands 2 worked with them to craft the game.

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:53.680
In this new game, Hyperion employee Jack&nbsp;
finds clues to a vault on a moon of Pandora,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:58.480
and hires 4 Vault Hunters to crack it open for&nbsp;
him. The 4 playable characters had all appeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:04.960
in previous games in one way or another, either as&nbsp;
bosses or NPCs, including series mascot Claptrap.

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:08.880
Pre-Sequel offered a few tweaks&nbsp;
to the known Borderlands formula,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:14.160
like adding new weapon types, vehicles like the&nbsp;
hovercraft, as well as low gravity areas and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:19.120
need to use O2 canisters for air, which would&nbsp;
let you double jump when you had them equipped.

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:22.560
Pre-Sequel didn’t set the world on&nbsp;
fire, with reviewers criticising the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:29.200
story and some repetition in the late game. It was&nbsp;
initially released for the PS3, Xbox 360, and PC,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:34.960
and was later brought to PS4, Xbox One and PC&nbsp;
as part of the Handsome Collection, bundled with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:41.120
Borderlands 2. 2K Australia was sadly shuttered&nbsp;
in 2015, a few months after the game’s launch.&nbsp;

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:57.200
In 2014, Telltale Games began to release Tales&nbsp;
from the Borderlands: an episodic adventure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.200 --> 00:10:02.560
game set in the Borderlands universe. The project&nbsp;
came about when Gearbox and Telltale were sitting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.560 --> 00:10:08.320
at neighbouring tables at the Spike Video Game&nbsp;
Awards in 2012. The two companies got to chatting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.320 --> 00:10:13.440
and over a few drinks, the idea to set a Telltale&nbsp;
game in the Borderlands universe came up.

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:17.040
While Tales from the Borderlands&nbsp;
did have some action in it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:24.720
it was a far cry from the bombastic&nbsp;
mayhem of the main series. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:29.680
fans still praised the story, its two&nbsp;
protagonists Rhys and Fiona, as well as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:35.680
the choice-driven gameplay. When Telltale Games&nbsp;
closed in 2018, the 5 episodes were pulled from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:45.840
sale until 2K managed to obtain the rights and&nbsp;
rereleased the series almost three years later.&nbsp;

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:54.080
After the release of Borderlands 1 and 2,&nbsp;
Gearbox was a little tired of the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:58.640
and so shifted its sights onto different&nbsp;
projects, including Battleborn, a hero&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:58.640 --> 00:11:04.320
shooter meets MOBA. Battleborn was not a success,&nbsp;
partly because it received middling reviews,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:10.080
and partly because Blizzard released its own&nbsp;
hero shooter, Overwatch just a few weeks later.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:13.840
Battleborn eventually closed down, but&nbsp;
it turned out the experience working on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:16.960
something new was just what&nbsp;
the team at Gearbox needed.

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:21.920
As is the Gearbox way, the team wanted to go&nbsp;
bigger and better with the third installment:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:26.160
no longer just centered on the planet&nbsp;
Pandora, Borderlands 3 allowed players,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:31.040
via their ship Sanctuary III, to traverse the&nbsp;
galaxy to find Vaults that were hidden on other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:36.240
planets before the Children of the Vault could.&nbsp;
After Handsome Jack’s defeat in Borderlands 2,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:41.440
a new power had risen in the form of a&nbsp;
cult loosely inspired by streamer culture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.440 --> 00:11:44.800
with its two leaders looking to&nbsp;
grab the vaults for themselves.

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:48.960
Like with previous titles, Borderlands&nbsp;
3 offered procedurally generated loot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:56.000
and promised over one billion guns for players to&nbsp;
potentially find. Co-op also received some tweaks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.000 --> 00:12:00.880
thanks to the Level Syncing system, everyone&nbsp;
could play together, regardless of their level,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:05.600
and each would be matched by level appropriate&nbsp;
enemies. And for those who hate squabbling over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:10.320
loot, you could set your game so that each&nbsp;
player would receive level-appropriate drops.

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:13.120
Borderlands 3 released in September 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:18.160
and received two season passes worth of&nbsp;
content, including game packs, new skill trees,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:18.160 --> 00:12:22.560
and a new game mode which was basically&nbsp;
a type of Borderlands Battle Royale.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:28.000
Thanks to an exclusivity deal with the Epic Games&nbsp;
Store, it was exclusive to that storefront on PC&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:32.560
for six months, leading to other games in&nbsp;
the series being review bombed on Steam.

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:41.120
Borderlands 3 was eagerly anticipated, and&nbsp;
the game even had a crossover with Fortnite.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.120 --> 00:12:46.640
It reviewed really well, expanding&nbsp;
the Borderlands gameplay formula,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:51.120
and offering payoffs for story beats that&nbsp;
fans had been following for a decade.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:56.560
As of the end of 2019, Borderlands 3 has&nbsp;
sold over 8 million copies, and its success&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:56.560 --> 00:13:01.920
helped the franchise hit over $1 billion.
Which brings us to Tiny Tina’s Wonderlands,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:07.200
which once again sees Tina in the role of&nbsp;
Bunkermaster as she guides you and your party&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:23.280
through an epic high-fantasy adventure. Instead&nbsp;
of choosing from a pre-made Vault hunter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:27.360
the game allows you to create your own&nbsp;
character, and mix and match your skills.

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:32.160
Not only can you use guns in the game, but&nbsp;
now you can use melee weapons like swords&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:36.320
as well as magic to fend off the hordes of&nbsp;
enemies you’ll be up against. The majority&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:39.680
of the action is in first-person,&nbsp;
but when traversing the overworld,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.680 --> 00:13:43.840
your characters turn into cute table&nbsp;
top miniature versions of themselves.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:49.040
The game also features a pretty high-profile&nbsp;
cast, including Andy Samberg and Will Arnett.&nbsp;

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:58.560
Which was your favourite Borderlands game? Let us&nbsp;
know in the comments, and make sure to subscribe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:58.560 --> 00:14:14.880
to GameSpot for more on Tiny Tina’s Wonderlands,&nbsp;
coming your way very soon. Thanks for watching!

